WEBVTT

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:41.230
<b>8. Vice Versa</b>

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:17.460
Lord Abel.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:21.570
The Captain wishes to know if you have any
specific instructions regarding our destination.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:27.120
I have determined
where they are headed.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:29.470
Set a north-northwesterly course.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:31.000
Very good, sir.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.570
Helena...

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.000
Good afternoon!

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:23.880
Er, g-good afternoon.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.390
Let me guess, you're lost too?

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.840
The same thing happened to me.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.390
That's why I was dancing.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:35.390
Um, why?

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:40.900
That's a good question!
I'm not really sure, either!

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:43.940
My name is Helena.

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:45.910
What's yours?

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:49.910
My name...

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:52.980
...is Abel.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.080
Abel Bluefield.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:01.540
Just so you know,
I'm supposedly a prince.

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:06.550
But they say I'll never be king.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:07.800
Oh, really?

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:10.650
I don't have any family.
Or friends.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.670
That sounds lonely.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:13.830
Yeah.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:15.940
I'm used to it, though.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:19.930
So, does that make me
your first friend?

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:40.390
Helena!

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:25.360
Have you heard
about Miss Helena?

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:29.280
They say she eloped with
a Dutchman named Franz

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:31.380
while carrying the king's child!

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:35.020
What'll happen to her
if she's found?

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.140
Executed! Put to death!

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:38.400
She'll be burned at the stake!

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:55.910
Lord Abel!

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:49.860
Helena!

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:52.780
Helena, why?

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:54.650
Why did you vanish?

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:56.530
Why did you leave me?

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:05.720
I wouldn't have cared if you were trying
to have a child with my father.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:08.340
I wanted you to be near me.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.670
That's all I wanted...

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:13.490
Without you,

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:17.300
I'd be all alone
in the world again.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:22.810
I don't want to be alone anymore.
Not again.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:25.450
Don't leave me!

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:27.930
I'm begging you!

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:31.440
That man told me.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.630
That man?
What man?

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:38.200
That butler? "Franz," I think?

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:42.010
"The father has to be him.

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:45.950
If the father is not a king,
La Pucelle cannot be born."

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:02.470
Don't cry, Abel Bluefield.

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:05.770
My part to play is now finished.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:09.350
Now, I just have to
return to Eden.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:11.860
Eden?

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:16.700
If I go there, will I be able
to see you again?

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:26.870
Those who have a calling
will be guided to Eden.

00:10:27.590 --> 00:10:31.970
I can't say for sure
if that is the case for you.

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:34.380
But...

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:38.380
...if you should ever cross paths
with the child,

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:42.850
perhaps that will mean
that you also have a calling.

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:52.340
Goodbye, Abel.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:57.530
You're the only person
I ever loved in this world.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:11.430
This place... holds nothing
for me now.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:26.780
Nothing... at all.

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:31.790
Wait for me, Helena.

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.050
I'll be with you soon.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.540
It's time, Alba Regina.

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:14.180
There's still a little pain.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:23.440
Do you need something?

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:29.990
- Feeling better?
- Nine on a scale of ten.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.950
Oh. That's good news.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.210
- The onigiri.
- About earlier...

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:37.830
Those there.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.170
Did you make them?

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:42.710
Um, yeah.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:44.720
What's in them?

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:48.680
This one's seaweed, this one's plum.
And this one is some kind of fish.

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:51.430
I'll have the fish, then.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:53.220
Be my guest.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.100
This is plum.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:01.110
Oh, sorry!
This one is the fish!

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:07.950
Um, listen, Yukimaru...

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:12.700
When you said what you said earlier,
what did you mean?

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:15.290
- What did I mean by what?
- That stuff you said! You know!

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:17.410
You'll have to be
more specific.

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:36.020
Okay, then...

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.690
The wind has picked up.
Let's go back in.

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:43.650
Um, I'm gonna stay here
a bit longer.

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:46.070
- Go on without me.
- All right.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:19.270
What came before is south snows,

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:22.690
in the hour of cold flame.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:26.730
Dark blue water,

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:30.740
white storm clouds.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:31.990
Yukimaru? That song, how--

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:33.700
The journey to the end...

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:37.370
- Where did you learn that song?
- From <i>you.</i>

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:41.170
You were singing it as you danced around
aboard the <i>Hope.</i>

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.830
You called it a secret song,
and you were belting it out.

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.630
I was shouting... a secret song?

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:49.420
You wouldn't stop singing it,
so it stuck in my head.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.680
Why don't <i>you</i> remember it?

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:54.600
I remember the melody,
but that's all.

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:58.310
I suppose it's no surprise,
the lyrics are gibberish.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:02.980
Yukimaru, do you remember
all of the lyrics?

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:04.980
Yes.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.820
More than golden,
the land of the gods.

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:11.530
Atop the lattice stage,
dance, o shrine maiden.

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:14.660
Far across the waves,
the maid slumbers.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:17.450
What came before is south snows,
in the hour of cold flame.

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:20.830
Dark blue water,
white storm clouds.

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:23.920
The journey to the end,
the stone that shows the way.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.420
What lies ahead
is the sun setting in the east.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:29.130
Now is the time to run,
beyond the ark.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:32.840
Beyond the ark...

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:35.260
Dark blue water...

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:37.760
...white storm clouds.

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:43.390
<i>Which wilt thou choose?
Blue water? Or storm clouds?</i>

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:47.360
Blue water or storm clouds.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:50.190
The maid slumbers.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:53.150
The stone that shows the way.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:55.200
The hour of cold flame.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:58.120
They match what
we've seen and done.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:16:59.540
Fena?

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:03.830
Do you suppose that maybe the words
to that song point the way to Eden?

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:07.840
When I first came to the island,
Yukihisa said something.

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:12.920
<i>Your father ought to have told you
about it in some way or another.</i>

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:18.350
O'Malley said that they needed
both the coordinates <i>and</i> me.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:22.680
<i>Apparently, we need both the girl
</i>and<i> the coordinates.</i>

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:28.400
If this song that was taught only to me
contains hints to the location of Eden, then...

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:33.190
What about "Atop the lattice stage,
dance, o shrine maiden"?

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:35.450
It's probably a place
we haven't been to yet.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:40.450
Fena, do you remember
the pedestal?

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.580
Hm? Yeah.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:47.250
That was almost certainly the face
of a clock, just as Karin suspected.

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:48.250
Yeah.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:51.590
The information they provide
are time and direction.

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:54.470
The stone only had time
etched into it.

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:56.590
Why was the direction
left out?

00:17:57.300 --> 00:18:00.470
Are we supposed to pair up that time
to the directions in the song's lyrics?

00:17:57.800 --> 00:18:00.470
SOUTH

00:17:57.800 --> 00:18:00.470
EAST

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:03.930
Even if that's the case,
there are two numbers.

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:07.980
There are "61" and "34,"
written in Roman numerals.

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:11.980
"What came before" is the past.
"What lies ahead" is the future.

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:11.980
"What came before"

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:11.980
"What lies ahead"

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:16.490
VI    I     PAST
FUTURE     III   IV

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:16.490
The sands of time flow from top to bottom.
In other words...

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:21.240
"South" is 61 degrees,
and "east" is 34 degrees?

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:22.950
That's what it must mean.

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:25.080
What's wrong?

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:28.500
It seems wrong somehow.
I can't explain why, though.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:33.250
Besides, the order is the reverse
of the places we visited.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:45.060
Fena?

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:47.890
I just remembered...

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.560
- I just remembered something!
- Remembered what?

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:54.820
The name of the song!
It's "Vice Versa"!

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:57.240
Vice Versa?

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:00.490
Latin for "the reverse
also holds true"...

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:02.450
Reverse...

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:07.830
I see! The answer
isn't south and east!

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:09.960
It's north and west!

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.130
Past and future
are also reversed!

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.840
In other words,
flipped vertically.

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:19.550
Sixty-one degrees west longitude.
Thirty-four degrees north latitude.

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:22.720
I think the numbers
might also be reversed.

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:28.350
That would also explain why they're in
Roman numerals instead of Arabic.

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:31.480
So...

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:36.730
Fourteen degrees west longitude,
63 degrees north latitude.

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:39.570
I bet that's where Eden is.

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:44.580
But we don't know for certain that this song
is really a hint to Eden's location.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:45.370
I think...

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:47.870
...that's probably reversed, too.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:50.500
I'm not looking for Eden.

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:52.620
Eden is making <i>me</i> look for <i>it.</i>

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:58.590
And when I've made the right choice,
someone comes to tell me.

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:00.510
Someone?

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:03.300
Yukimaru. Let's go.

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:05.010
Back to the others.

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:12.690
Everything is in place.
Now you just have to choose.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:31.540
"The reverse also holds true"...

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:32.960
Well, I'll be...

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:35.670
- Virgin bursar...
- Vice versa!

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:38.590
This location isn't all that far away.

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:40.340
It certainly isn't.

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:41.550
Yukimaru.

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:45.470
- How are the injuries?
- I'll be fine.

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:46.680
Shitan.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:50.430
Are we good?

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:54.650
Yes, we're good.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:13.160
All sorts of things
happened to me.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:15.580
I never knew why,
so I didn't know what to do.

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:19.840
But all those answers
can be found at Eden.

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:21.710
That's what I've
come to believe.

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:26.220
Because Eden is the thing
that brought me to all of you.

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:31.470
I know that it might mean making
a bunch of trouble for you again.

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:34.690
But I want to see all sorts
of places with you!

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.730
I want to travel with you all!

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:40.610
I don't know what's waiting
for us up ahead.

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:44.610
But I want you to put your faith
in me and follow me!

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:47.610
Set course for... Eden!

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:51.120
- Let's go there together!
- Yeah!

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:54.870
- A bunch of trouble, huh?
- Not like that's anything new.

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:57.370
Fena is hopeless without
me around, you know?

00:21:57.500 --> 00:21:59.750
This is shaping up to be
another rowdy trip.

00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:03.130
- First things first! Food!
- Shopping trip!
